 \label{subsec:ch7_scan}
 
+Large $\pT^\tau$ and $\met$ are more characteristic of heavy-leptoquark production than of the bulk of the $W$+jets and top-quark backgrounds.
+Lower thresholds on both quantities therefore improve the signal-to-background ratio.
+
+The $\mT$ distribution from on-shell $W\to\tau\nu$ decays is bounded by the $W$-boson mass for correctly reconstructed momenta and no additional source of $\mpt$.
+Off-shell $W$ production, additional neutrinos and detector resolution generate a high-$\mT$ background tail, which can be enhanced by non-resonant leptoquark exchange.
+A lower $\mT$ threshold targets this signal contribution.
+
+The invariant masses $m_{b\tau}$ and $m_{j\tau}$ probe resonant $U_1\to b\tau$ and $U_1\to s\tau$ decays, respectively, while the SM backgrounds have no corresponding heavy resonance.
+The $\tau$-decay neutrino shifts the signal distributions below $\MU$ and broadens them, with additional smearing from the jet and $\tau$ energy resolutions.
+A lower mass threshold suppresses the SM backgrounds while retaining this broad signal.
+
+The separation $\DphiTauMet$ tends towards $\pi$ in non-resonant production with a soft recoiling jet, whereas top-quark events have more complex decay kinematics.
+A lower threshold favours this signal geometry; an upper threshold is also tested for resonant production, where the energetic decay jet changes the transverse momentum balance.
+
+The jet multiplicity $N_j-N_b$ tends to be larger in $\ttbar$ events because the two top-quark decays produce additional jets.
+An upper limit suppresses this background while retaining signal events with fewer jets.
+
 The kinematic thresholds are scanned together because the discriminating variables are correlated.
 For example, increasing $\met$ also raises $\mT$ at fixed $\pT^\tau$ and $\DphiTauMet$, so the effect of an additional $\mT$ requirement depends on the other cuts.
+
 Lower thresholds on $\pT^\tau$, $\met$ and $\mT$ are scanned in both categories, together with an upper limit on $N_j-N_b$.
 A lower threshold on $\DphiTauMet$ is tested for the non-resonant topology.
-For the resonant topology, upper thresholds on this angle and a lower threshold on $m_{b\tau}$ are tested.
